  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">You train and empower your dracoleum pathways to make your breath weapon more devastating. Your Draichsar Breath doubles its range, to a 60-foot line or a 30-foot cone, and its damage die increases to d6s instead of d4s. On a critical failure on a saving throw, you apply the critical weapon specialization effect to the creature. If your damage type is vitality or void, you add 2d6 persistent damage of that type on a critical failure.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Special</span></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> If you have the Dracoleum Glob feat, its area also is doubled to a 20-foot burst.</span></p>"
